1935.stem:
A shape consists of three sides of a square together with a sector, $ODC$, where $O$ is the midpoint of $AB$, as shown below (not to scale).

$DA=AB=BC=2$ cm

\exfigure{402_q11_1}

solutions.latex:
$O$ is the midpoint of $AB$, so $AO=1$. In the right-angled triangle $DAO$, Pythagoras' theorem gives
$$\begin{aligned}DO&=\sqrt{2^2+1^2} \\ &=\sqrt{5}\text{ cm}\end{aligned}$$
\exfigure{402_q11_s1}

In $\triangle DOC$, $DO=\sqrt{5}$ from part (a), $OC=\sqrt{5}$ (right-angled triangle $OBC$ with $OB=1$ and $BC=2$), and $DC=2$. By the cosine rule:
$$\begin{aligned}\cos\theta&=\dfrac{DO^2+OC^2-DC^2}{2\times DO\times OC} \\ &=\dfrac{(\sqrt{5})^2+(\sqrt{5})^2-2^2}{2(\sqrt{5})(\sqrt{5})} \\ &=\dfrac{6}{10} \\ &=\dfrac{3}{5}\end{aligned}$$
\exfigure{402_q11_s2}

